The native bundle has no libmariadbd dynamic dependency: MariaDB and the C
wrapper are compiled into the WASM/AOT guest. Python communicates with the Go
host, which uses a separate Wasmer process. The project chooses GPL-2.0-only
for its own code rather than claiming this process boundary exempts all parts.

License texts are in licenses/. This list is not yet a complete SBOM of the
prebuilt Wasmer release or the WASIX sysroot. Do not treat this local alpha as
ready for public release merely because a wheel can be built.
